            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The hour of sudden divine intervention, unexpected judgment, and the unanticipated return of Christ, often marking a climactic transition from darkness to deliverance.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Matthew 25:6\",\"Exodus 12:29\",\"Mark 13:35\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A period of deep spiritual darkness, human ignorance, or the peak of worldly sin before the light of Christ.\",\"basis\":[\"Romans 13:12\",\"1 Thessalonians 5:7\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"An hour of urgent intercession, desperate prayer, and unexpected breakthrough or deliverance in the midst of trials.\",\"basis\":[\"Luke 11:5-8\",\"Acts 16:25\",\"Psalm 119:62\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The dominant eschatological symbolism is derived largely from the Parable of the Ten Virgins and the Exodus Passover account, establishing midnight as the archetypal moment of sudden visitation requiring constant spiritual vigilance.\"}",
